                <pb facs="0277" n="271" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg271"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Merrill.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 127.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27,
                        1889</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 241 of the 8th
                    instant, representing the circumstances under which you regard it advisable for
                    a United States ship of war to remain for the present in Hawaiian waters.</p>
                <p>A copy of your dispatch has been submitted for the consideration of the Secretary
                    of the Navy.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
